# Duplicate-labelset guard on a label REWRITE (#1839).
#
# `label_replace(v, "dst", "<const>", "src", ".*")` overwrites `dst` with a
# constant on every input series. Two series that differed ONLY in `dst`
# therefore land on one label set — and unlike the name-drop half, their
# `__name__` values are EQUAL, so `uniqExact(MetricName) > 1` would answer
# 1 and wave the collision through. The rewrite guard counts ROWS per
# output identity instead: `throwIf(count() > 1, …) = 0` grouped by the
# identity the rewrite PRESERVES, which here is (Attributes, MetricName).
#
# Upstream reaches the same verdict from the same generic per-step site as
# every other shape (prometheus/promql/engine.go:1531, :1552) — it does not
# special-case label_replace, and neither does the message.
#
# The group key reads the REWRITTEN Attributes, which is why the guard sits
# ABOVE the rewrite Project rather than below it: grouping the pre-rewrite
# column would check the label set the query is moving away from.
#
# The outer canonical 4-column Project is load-bearing. A `chplan.Aggregate`
# is classified derived-shape, and the HTTP layer stamps an empty
# MetricName over a derived shape — which would silently discard the name
# `label_replace` deliberately preserves. Naming all four canonical outputs
# restores the classification.
#
# Seedless for the same reason as
# rate_multi_name_duplicate_labelset_guard.txtar: the round-trip runner has
# no shape for an expected error. The executable half is in
# internal/api/prom/handler_chdb_duplicate_labelset_test.go.
-- query.promql --
label_replace(cpu_temp, "core", "all", "core", ".*")
-- parity_exempt --
reason: rejection-only
detail: This query must be REJECTED (HTTP 422); it carries no seed/expected_rows because the round-trip runner has no shape for an expected error. The executable assertion lives in internal/api/prom/handler_chdb_duplicate_labelset_test.go, not in a value comparison RunParity could perform.
